    "faq": {
      "type": "bottom-faq",
      "blocks": {
        "fq1": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is nattokinase derived from?",
            "content": "<p>Nattokinase is a serine-protease enzyme extracted from natto, a traditional Japanese fermented soybean food. It is produced by the Bacillus subtilis var. natto bacterium during the fermentation process. Discovered in Tokyo in 1980 by Dr. Hiroyuki Sumi, it has been studied for over 40 years for its fibrinolytic activity.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq2": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How does nattokinase work?",
            "content": "<p>Nattokinase is a serine protease — a protein-cutting enzyme — that acts directly on fibrin (the protein mesh in blood clots) and inactivates PAI-1, the body's natural brake on fibrin clearance. In vitro studies also show it degrades the SARS-CoV-2 spike protein (Tanikawa 2022) and fibrinaloid microclots associated with Long COVID (Grixti/Kell 2024 preprint). In a 12-month human trial (Chen 2022, n=1,062), cardiovascular markers improved significantly at 6,000–12,000 FU/day.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq3": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What is spike protein and why does it matter?",
            "content": "<p>The spike protein is the surface protein of the SARS-CoV-2 coronavirus that binds to ACE2 receptors in human cells. Post-viral researchers have documented spike protein persistence in some individuals after infection or vaccination. In vitro studies have examined nattokinase's ability to degrade this protein (Tanikawa 2022, Molecules). These are laboratory studies — not in vivo human trials — but they explain why spike-detox protocols have gained traction in the post-viral community.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq4": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Are there clinical studies on the ingredients in Complete?",
            "content": "<p><em>Nattokinase:</em> Chen et al. 2022, <em>Frontiers in Cardiovascular Medicine</em>. <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9458005/\">PMC9458005</a></p><p><em>Bromelain:</em> Pavan et al. 2012, <em>Biomed Res Int</em>. <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC3529416/\">PMC3529416</a></p><p><em>NAC:</em> Izquierdo et al. 2022, <em>Sci Rep</em>. <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8915136/\">PMC8915136</a></p><p><em>Quercetin:</em> Di Pierro et al. 2021, <em>Int J Gen Med</em>. <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC8403043/\">PMC8403043</a></p><p><em>Tanikawa 2022 (spike protein, in vitro):</em> <a href=\"https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC9457822/\">PMC9457822</a></p><p><em>BioPerine:</em> Shoba et al. 1998, PMID 9619120</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq5": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How do I take Spike Detox Complete?",
            "content": "<p>4 capsules per day, split into two doses: <strong>2 caps before breakfast on an empty stomach, 2 caps mid-afternoon</strong> at least 2 hours after lunch. Empty-stomach timing matters for the proteolytic enzymes. Lower-intensity onboarding: 2 caps/day for the first 2 weeks, then titrate to 4.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq6": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "How many servings per bottle?",
            "content": "<p>Each bottle contains 120 capsules. At the recommended dose of 4 capsules/day, that is a 30-day supply. At 2 capsules/day (onboarding or lower-intensity protocol), the bottle lasts 60 days.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq7": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Is it allergen-free?",
            "content": "<p>Nattokinase is derived from fermented soybeans — individuals with soy allergies should consult their physician before use. The capsule shell is vegan (HPMC). There are no gluten, dairy, egg, nut, or shellfish ingredients in the formula. No synthetic dyes or unnecessary fillers.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq8": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "What size are the capsules?",
            "content": "<p>Size 00 HPMC (vegetarian/vegan) capsules. They are larger than a standard size 0, which allows us to deliver the full 7-active formula in a single capsule without fillers padding out the volume.</p>"
          }
        },
        "fq9": {
          "type": "faq",
          "settings": {
            "title": "Important disclosures — shelf life, storage, and FDA statement",
            "content": "<p>Shelf life: 24 months from manufacture date printed on the bottle. Store in a cool, dry place away from direct sunlight. Refrigeration is not required but will not harm the product.</p><p><em>These statements have not been evaluated by the Food and Drug Administration. This product is not intended to diagnose, treat, cure, or prevent any disease.</em></p><p><em>Consult your healthcare provider before use, especially if you take blood-thinning medication, are pregnant or nursing, or have a bleeding disorder.</em></p>"
          }
        }
      },
